{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ vogue diversity success popularity)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1879822902#5_3004290619","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q337","rank":2,"snippet":"but to return to modeling. She’s been featured in many print ads. Several designers had her on the catwalk during Fashion Week in her 80s! Today, she is proba­bly THE most famous model over 60. Maye Musk Canadian Maye has been modeling since she was just 15. (Her children have also enjoyed <cover>success. One of her sons is Elon Musk, inventor of the cutting-edge car, the Tesla.) Maye’s look is somewhat edgy as she often sports a very modern short haircut that designers love. Maye always looks like she’s having fun and she probably is. Even she marvels at her popularity as she turns 70 this year. Beverly Johnson Beverly, now 65, was the first African American woman to grace the cover of Vogue Magazine in 1974. She was 21 at the time and has been modeling ever since. Diversity </cover>has contin­ued to be a vital issue in the fashion world. The New York Times named Johnson one of the 20th century’s most influential people in fashion in 2008. YAZEMEENAH ROSSI Pia Gronning Pia, 68, is from Denmark and also an actress. she has that stunning Scandinavian blonde hair blue-eyed look that ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1879822902#6_3004295058","rank":1,"relevance":1}]}}
