{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"teen vogue\" \"social justice\" (+ traffic readership audience growth popular))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_1422883952#5_3212085886","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q367","rank":2,"snippet":"Johnson ran as the Libertarian presidential candidate. A number of little-known Libertarian candidates are currently running in the 2020 presidential primaries. 2. Green Party Founded in the early 1980s, the Green Party’s main focus is environmentalism. Other priorities include nonviolence, <cover>social justice, and gender equality, according to its website. During the 2012 and 2016 elections, the party ran Jill Stein as its presidential candidate. According to a recent New York Times article, Stein has “no plans” to run a third time. Still, she drew attention to the party with her platform of addressing the climate crisis and establishing Medicare for All, earning about 1.07% of the presidential popular vote in 2016. The Green Party remains one of the three minor parties recognized by more than 10 states as of May 2018. According to the Times, party leaders say they’ve gained over 39,000 registered Greens since July 2016.\" , \"start_char\": 3217.000000 , \"title\": \"Alternatives to the Two Major Political Parties, Explained | Teen Vogue</cover>\" , \"url\": \"https://www.teenvogue.com/story/alternatives-to-two-major-political-parties-explained\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_439907463#8_476374388","rank":1,"relevance":2}]}}
